WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.040 --> 00:02.240
This series was created for entertainment purposes.

3
00:02.240 --> 00:05.680
The characters, actions, locations, dialogue, languages, ceremonies,

4
00:05.680 --> 00:08.120
and artistic elements depicted in this series

5
00:08.120 --> 00:10.040
are fictional and based on imagination,

6
00:10.040 --> 00:13.920
incorporating the beauty of the region's diverse cultures,

7
00:13.920 --> 00:18.400
including those of Lanna, Myanmar, the Tai peoples, and China.

8
00:18.400 --> 00:20.560
It is not intended to disrespect any history,

9
00:20.560 --> 00:23.600
ethnic group, organization, profession, or group of individuals.

10
00:23.600 --> 00:26.040
Viewer discretion is advised.

11
00:26.040 --> 00:28.160
[Previously] You've finally returned to Wiang Kaew.

12
00:28.160 --> 00:31.560
But your stay is only temporary, Your Highness.

13
00:31.560 --> 00:33.760
I'll do everything I can to win Father's approval,

14
00:33.760 --> 00:36.720
so I can stay in Ullavee for good.

15
00:36.720 --> 00:41.680
Princess Maneethip did have a lover, just as you suspected.

16
00:41.680 --> 00:44.600
Then tell me what happened to General In Saeng?

17
00:44.600 --> 00:46.800
General In Saeng...

18
00:46.800 --> 00:50.440
died of jungle fever two days ago while stationed at the border.

19
00:50.440 --> 00:54.040
From now on, you must watch your every move.

20
00:54.040 --> 00:56.520
Remember everything I've taught you.

21
00:56.520 --> 00:59.600
- You'll be presented to the King tomorrow. - Yes.

22
01:24.720 --> 01:28.800
- Dried peep flowers, my lady. - This tobacco blend is called Kiyo.

23
01:28.800 --> 01:32.560
It's made with loose tobacco, ground tamarind bark,

24
01:32.560 --> 01:35.520
and dried peep flowers.

25
01:35.520 --> 01:37.760
The King is very fond of this blend.

26
01:37.760 --> 01:42.360
It soothes the throat when smoked, and leaves the breath smelling fresh.

27
01:43.080 --> 01:48.680
You'll be helping me roll tobacco by hand, and prepare leaf wraps.

28
01:48.680 --> 01:54.400
You'll also serve tea, snacks, and drinks to the King.

29
01:55.080 --> 01:59.440
- I'm nervous. I'm afraid I'll make mistakes. - There's nothing to fear.

30
01:59.440 --> 02:04.480
Just follow what I've taught you, and you'll be fine.

31
02:06.480 --> 02:10.800
Wiang Kaew can bring you as much harm as it can bring you gain.

32
02:10.800 --> 02:12.880
So be wise.

33
02:12.880 --> 02:16.520
Don't even think of doing anything you shouldn't.

34
02:34.480 --> 02:37.720
Lady Homjan and Fongnuan have come to serve Your Majesty.

35
02:37.720 --> 02:39.160
Come in.

36
04:22.080 --> 04:28.520
[Tears of Love]

37
04:35.840 --> 04:39.960
Breathe in. Breathe out.

38
04:39.960 --> 04:44.200
Breathe in. Breathe out.

39
04:44.200 --> 04:48.080
Breathe in. Breathe out.

40
04:49.880 --> 04:53.160
- I pay my respects to you, Your Majesty. - I pay my respects to you, Your Majesty.

41
04:57.520 --> 05:02.480
I've brought the new lady-in-waiting to serve Your Majesty.

42
05:43.680 --> 05:46.000
I am Fongnuan.

43
05:46.800 --> 05:50.440
I've prepared leaf wraps and hand-rolled Kiyo for Your Majesty.

44
05:51.560 --> 05:53.160
Did you make these yourself?

45
05:55.080 --> 05:56.360
Yes, Your Majesty.

46
05:57.600 --> 06:02.080
Had you not told me, I'd have thought Homjan made them.

47
06:06.520 --> 06:11.600
I'm not nearly as skilled as Lady Homjan, Your Majesty.

48
06:13.800 --> 06:18.560
Your new apprentice is a quick learner.

49
06:18.560 --> 06:21.560
And modest, too.

50
06:21.560 --> 06:24.800
You must be pleased with her, Homjan.

51
06:24.800 --> 06:30.480
She still has much to learn, Your Majesty. Please forgive her if she makes mistakes.

52
06:30.480 --> 06:35.640
I'll make sure she meets Your Majesty's expectations.

53
06:35.640 --> 06:38.360
Fongnuan, look at your Head Lady-in-Waiting.

54
06:38.360 --> 06:44.160
It's only your first day, and she's already defending you.

55
06:45.960 --> 06:51.320
Fongnuan doesn't ask for much, Your Majesty. But she's eager to learn.

56
06:51.320 --> 06:52.840
On her first day at Wiang Kaew,

57
06:52.840 --> 06:56.160
she made it clear she had no desire for a high position.

58
06:56.160 --> 06:59.200
She only wants to get through each day.

59
07:01.280 --> 07:06.000
Homjan tells me you know acupressure.

60
07:06.000 --> 07:09.120
I've been having pain in my neck and shoulders.

61
07:09.120 --> 07:11.720
Sometimes the pain reaches my head.

62
07:11.720 --> 07:16.000
Do you think you could help ease it?

63
07:28.120 --> 07:30.760
If Your Majesty permits,

64
07:30.760 --> 07:36.040
I'll do everything I can to help.

65
07:51.000 --> 07:55.400
The King's body is sacred. He possesses immense spiritual power.

66
07:55.400 --> 08:00.160
His body is protected by incantations. Not just anyone may touch him.

67
08:00.160 --> 08:05.680
That is why the King's physicians and masseurs are all men.

68
08:06.560 --> 08:11.440
As a woman, you must first offer popped rice and flowers.

69
08:11.440 --> 08:13.800
Ask permission and forgiveness for any offense.

70
08:13.800 --> 08:19.120
Otherwise, if his power overwhelms you, it could enter your body and harm you.

71
08:26.520 --> 08:31.840
My lady, what if I accidentally hurt the King?

72
08:31.840 --> 08:34.280
Will I be executed?

73
08:35.520 --> 08:38.800
Be very careful. Don't press the wrong spot.

74
09:40.280 --> 09:42.360
You've only pressed a few points,

75
09:44.000 --> 09:48.920
yet the pain and tension in my head have already eased.

76
09:50.800 --> 09:54.640
That is a valuable skill. I'm pleased.

77
10:20.880 --> 10:24.480
What are you doing about the bandits stealing from the granaries?

78
10:24.480 --> 10:29.080
I've sent soldiers to patrol the area, and keep a close watch on the granaries.

79
10:29.080 --> 10:32.400
I assure you it won't happen again.

80
10:33.720 --> 10:35.520
That's not enough.

81
10:36.160 --> 10:38.320
You must plan further ahead.

82
10:40.160 --> 10:45.360
The dry season is almost over. We must do more than guard the granaries.

83
10:46.200 --> 10:49.600
We must prepare for the rainy season...

84
10:49.600 --> 10:53.480
and ensure Ullavee has enough food and supplies

85
10:53.480 --> 10:55.600
to last the entire year.

86
10:59.520 --> 11:04.800
Thank you for your guidance, Father. I still have much to learn from you.

87
11:31.520 --> 11:36.560
The drum sounds once, marking the third watch.

88
11:39.000 --> 11:40.840
It's already half past one.

89
11:41.920 --> 11:44.760
Another important part of your duty...

90
11:44.760 --> 11:47.880
is looking after His Majesty's health.

91
11:47.880 --> 11:50.880
You must help me care for him and watch over him.

92
11:50.880 --> 11:56.280
Make sure he doesn't fall ill or do anything that harms his health.

93
11:57.360 --> 12:00.000
I pay my respects to you, Your Majesty.

94
12:11.080 --> 12:15.600
The drum has sounded, marking the third watch.

95
12:16.720 --> 12:21.640
Your Majesty's yawning tells me...

96
12:21.640 --> 12:26.280
it's time for you to rest.

97
12:38.000 --> 12:43.240
If Your Majesty doesn't get enough sleep, your health will suffer.

98
12:43.240 --> 12:44.800
The less you sleep,

99
12:44.800 --> 12:49.520
the weaker your body and immune system become.

100
12:49.520 --> 12:51.440
You'll be more prone to illness.

101
12:51.440 --> 12:56.120
Your memory and ability to think may also suffer, Your Majesty.

102
12:56.920 --> 13:01.200
How do you know that? Have you studied traditional medicine?

103
13:11.160 --> 13:15.400
A traditional healer in Wang Nam Lin once told me my mother...

104
13:15.400 --> 13:17.880
fell ill from not getting enough sleep.

105
13:17.880 --> 13:20.320
I've never forgotten it, Your Majesty.

106
13:31.720 --> 13:33.560
Let us retire for the night.

107
13:34.760 --> 13:40.480
I don't want anyone falling ill from staying up late on my account.

108
13:42.720 --> 13:44.520
You may go and rest.

109
14:10.200 --> 14:12.400
I'm worried that

110
14:12.400 --> 14:19.320
if Fongnuan, Saen Thep's wife's cousin, becomes Father's favorite,

111
14:19.320 --> 14:23.920
your position as Crown Prince could be threatened.

112
14:37.520 --> 14:40.800
- I pay my respects to you, Your Majesty. - I pay my respects to you, Your Majesty.

113
15:18.720 --> 15:20.200
Fongnuan.

114
15:38.000 --> 15:41.560
You're fortunate His Majesty wasn't offended tonight,

115
15:41.560 --> 15:45.040
but you must be more careful with what you say from now on.

116
15:47.720 --> 15:52.480
Forgive me for speaking out of turn.

117
15:57.400 --> 16:03.160
You told me my duty was to care for the King.

118
16:05.040 --> 16:09.240
If he fell ill from working late,

119
16:09.240 --> 16:14.560
I'd have failed in my duty.

120
16:15.400 --> 16:19.160
Besides, you looked exhausted yourself.

121
16:19.160 --> 16:23.880
I couldn't let either you...

122
16:23.880 --> 16:26.000
or His Majesty fall ill.

123
16:27.000 --> 16:29.920
Don't use me as an excuse.

124
16:30.680 --> 16:34.200
- Are you trying to flatter me? - No, my lady.

125
16:35.240 --> 16:38.200
I'm genuinely concerned about you.

126
16:43.360 --> 16:46.440
I'm worried about myself, too.

127
16:47.600 --> 16:52.120
If anything happened to you, I'd be in trouble.

128
16:54.200 --> 16:55.920
I like your honesty.

129
16:57.040 --> 17:00.280
You never cease to surprise me.

130
17:03.080 --> 17:08.200
But this is Wiang Kaew. One wrong word could cost you your life.

131
17:08.200 --> 17:09.680
Remember that.

132
17:12.560 --> 17:13.960
Yes, my lady.

133
17:15.360 --> 17:18.240
Why must I keep an eye on Fongnuan?

134
17:18.240 --> 17:22.040
She's only a lady-in-waiting. She hardly seems dangerous.

135
17:22.040 --> 17:24.080
She's only a lady-in-waiting?

136
17:24.080 --> 17:27.480
How dare she tell the King when to stop working and go to bed?

137
17:29.040 --> 17:32.880
An ordinary lady-in-waiting would've been executed for that.

138
17:36.880 --> 17:39.960
Fongnuan has barely arrived at Wiang Kaew,

139
17:39.960 --> 17:43.120
yet Father already trusts her and has grown fond of her.

140
17:44.760 --> 17:46.440
I don't trust her.

141
17:47.880 --> 17:51.000
I don't want Father to take another royal consort.

142
17:55.480 --> 17:58.400
Father was probably just tired and wanted to rest.

143
17:58.400 --> 18:00.120
Stop defending her.

144
18:02.160 --> 18:04.960
We still don't know where her loyalties lie.

145
18:05.520 --> 18:09.680
Homjan may have sent her to win Father's favor for Kong Tai and Fah Haam,

146
18:10.680 --> 18:13.680
or Chiang La-or may be using her to help Saen Thep gain power.

147
18:15.120 --> 18:20.560
Whichever side she's on, I don't want another rival.

148
18:30.840 --> 18:33.440
Remember, she's the cousin of Saen Thep's wife.

149
18:34.920 --> 18:37.360
If I find out she's plotting anything,

150
18:39.280 --> 18:41.080
I won't spare her.

151
19:21.680 --> 19:23.560
These orchids...

152
19:25.480 --> 19:28.240
will bloom in my heart...

153
19:28.240 --> 19:30.640
until my dying breath.

154
20:21.560 --> 20:27.000
Has Princess Maneethip heard the news about General In Saeng?

155
20:40.840 --> 20:43.680
I've learned about Maneethip and General In Saeng.

156
20:47.240 --> 20:50.840
Don't be afraid to tell me the truth.

157
20:54.360 --> 20:57.360
I apologize on Princess Maneethip's behalf.

158
21:00.840 --> 21:03.320
She never meant to lie to you.

159
21:05.600 --> 21:09.400
She's been suffering over this all along.

160
21:10.880 --> 21:13.320
Please don't be angry with her.

161
21:26.160 --> 21:27.720
Don't be afraid.

162
21:29.600 --> 21:31.200
I understand.

163
21:33.800 --> 21:35.960
If anyone is to blame,

164
21:37.800 --> 21:39.760
I'm partly responsible.

165
22:01.120 --> 22:03.320
I'm going to Wiang Kaew today.

166
22:04.280 --> 22:09.120
Please make sure she eats when she wakes up.

167
22:09.880 --> 22:11.880
She hasn't eaten for days.

168
22:13.800 --> 22:15.160
I'm worried about her.

169
22:18.440 --> 22:19.720
Your Highness.

170
23:29.320 --> 23:31.200
I don't want to train.

171
23:31.840 --> 23:35.600
I don't like violence. I don't like using force.

172
23:36.920 --> 23:39.280
Come on, Kong Tai.

173
23:45.000 --> 23:46.320
What's this?

174
23:48.000 --> 23:51.960
Why is the training so brutal? I want no part of this.

175
23:51.960 --> 23:53.720
It's not worth dying for.

176
24:42.840 --> 24:44.160
A woman?

177
24:45.360 --> 24:46.840
Dao Kaew.

178
24:48.160 --> 24:50.600
Dao Kaew? You know her?

179
24:51.560 --> 24:54.600
Dao Kaew is Muen In's daughter.

180
24:55.400 --> 24:58.840
She's fought alongside her father and me.

181
24:58.840 --> 25:00.720
Of course I know her.

182
25:09.720 --> 25:13.800
What? Muen In lets his daughter go to war?

183
25:14.720 --> 25:18.240
He tried to stop her, but she wouldn't listen.

184
25:18.240 --> 25:21.920
She chose to live at the border, and fight in the war.

185
25:21.920 --> 25:26.080
She's no good at household chores. Fighting is what she does best.

186
25:29.760 --> 25:34.320
She's a better fighter than almost anyone in the army.

187
25:39.160 --> 25:41.240
Muen In's daughter...

188
25:54.240 --> 25:57.960
- Why are you smiling, Brother? - I'm not.

189
25:57.960 --> 26:00.760
- Are you training today or not? - Of course.

190
26:00.760 --> 26:03.880
It's my duty. How could I refuse?

191
26:03.880 --> 26:06.480
I thought you didn't like violence.

192
26:06.480 --> 26:10.080
Being a soldier means fighting. We must do our best to defend our homeland.

193
26:10.080 --> 26:15.760
I must always be ready to defend it. Remember that.

194
26:17.200 --> 26:20.880
What are you waiting for? I'm ready. Help me put on my armor.

195
26:25.720 --> 26:29.160
- Something must be going on. - Yes.

196
26:29.960 --> 26:34.360
Dao Kaew rarely comes into the city. What brings her here?

197
27:09.000 --> 27:10.800
Prince Saen Thep.

198
27:32.320 --> 27:36.280
I saw this and thought of you.

199
27:38.440 --> 27:40.600
Perhaps it'll keep you company when you're lonely.

200
27:41.840 --> 27:43.440
Thank you.

201
27:45.400 --> 27:49.800
I haven't had time to feel lonely. There's so much work to do.

202
27:49.800 --> 27:51.960
I'm drowning in work!

203
27:55.840 --> 27:58.760
There I go using strange expressions again.

204
27:58.760 --> 28:00.200
That's good.

205
28:00.920 --> 28:03.000
You make me laugh.

206
28:03.000 --> 28:08.240
I haven't laughed once since you moved into Wiang Kaew.

207
28:08.240 --> 28:10.160
I never thought...

208
28:10.160 --> 28:15.200
my silly remarks could be of use.

209
28:19.240 --> 28:22.480
I have a meeting with Muen In and Seer Phrommaya.

210
28:24.120 --> 28:27.360
I'll be serving tea at that meeting.

211
28:28.000 --> 28:30.040
Lady Homjan ordered me to.

212
28:30.040 --> 28:33.480
Since I know all the princes,

213
28:33.480 --> 28:36.840
she asked me to attend to you during the meeting.

214
28:38.520 --> 28:40.200
Then come with me.

215
28:40.200 --> 28:44.480
Not yet. I need to prepare the tea first.

216
28:45.920 --> 28:47.520
Let me help you.

217
29:10.720 --> 29:12.760
Did you know?

218
29:12.760 --> 29:16.200
Kong Tai loves this tea.

219
29:18.320 --> 29:22.000
What about you, Your Highness? Do you like it?

220
29:23.520 --> 29:25.080
I do.

221
29:25.080 --> 29:27.240
Then have as much as you like.

222
30:19.920 --> 30:21.640
Please stop playing for a moment.

223
30:29.400 --> 30:31.720
What's gotten into Prince Kong Tai?

224
30:36.280 --> 30:38.640
He's showing all the signs of being in love.

225
30:41.120 --> 30:47.080
Kong Tai has met the woman of his dreams. He's just found out she's Muen In's daughter.

226
30:49.360 --> 30:52.840
I see. The general's daughter.

227
31:03.920 --> 31:06.800
Hey! Why are you taking that away?

228
31:06.800 --> 31:11.200
Well, you were smiling to yourself, staring dreamily at my rice.

229
31:11.200 --> 31:13.600
I thought you must be full.

230
31:13.600 --> 31:17.240
I've barely eaten anything! How could I be full?

231
31:17.240 --> 31:22.440
Your heart is already full of thoughts of Muen In's daughter.

232
31:23.520 --> 31:26.800
Wait, you know about Dao Kaew?

233
31:32.640 --> 31:34.760
So you admit it!

234
31:35.600 --> 31:39.640
- If you're full, I'll eat it myself. - Wait!

235
31:40.880 --> 31:44.440
My heart may be full, but my stomach isn't!

236
31:44.440 --> 31:48.800
The happier I feel, the better your food tastes.

237
31:48.800 --> 31:51.960
I'll eat every last bite. Please do.

238
31:52.840 --> 31:54.920
Let's see how long...

239
31:54.920 --> 31:59.360
you'll keep coming back for my food.

240
31:59.360 --> 32:00.960
Until the day I die.

241
32:00.960 --> 32:06.960
Even after I'm married, I'll come back for your cooking every day.

242
32:09.520 --> 32:13.320
Being in love is wonderful, isn't it?

243
32:16.160 --> 32:20.200
That sticky rice looks sweet. Let me have some.

244
32:21.480 --> 32:23.400
Eat your own.

245
32:25.360 --> 32:28.080
Look! He's taking mine!

246
32:29.520 --> 32:33.880
Who's getting married again? You're bickering like children.

247
32:36.280 --> 32:38.120
Let me try some.

248
32:42.880 --> 32:47.680
Prince Fah Haam. This sticky rice tastes terribly bitter.

249
32:49.200 --> 32:51.120
Come on.

250
32:56.400 --> 32:58.400
It tastes sweet to me.

251
33:08.320 --> 33:11.200
Have you heard about General In Saeng?

252
33:16.080 --> 33:17.720
Your Highness...

253
33:19.880 --> 33:22.000
You know about him?

254
33:31.240 --> 33:32.920
He's dead.

255
33:40.880 --> 33:42.560
Has my cousin...

256
33:44.120 --> 33:46.240
heard the news?

257
33:54.320 --> 33:57.360
At least I finally know the truth.

258
34:00.080 --> 34:02.480
Maneethip should've told me from the start.

259
34:03.320 --> 34:07.200
If I'd known, I would've stepped aside.

260
34:09.120 --> 34:11.920
I don't have to get everything I want.

261
34:14.360 --> 34:15.960
My cousin...

262
34:17.240 --> 34:19.480
is the princess of Wang Nam Lin.

263
34:20.680 --> 34:25.560
She kept it from you because she had a duty to fulfill.

264
34:25.560 --> 34:27.680
But she also owed me the truth.

265
34:28.320 --> 34:30.920
That's part of her duty as my consort.

266
34:40.040 --> 34:41.720
Your Highness,

267
34:44.840 --> 34:50.320
suppose you had a daughter one day.

268
34:51.480 --> 34:57.400
You wanted her to marry...

269
34:59.040 --> 35:02.800
as her duty required, for the sake of her kingdom.

270
35:05.400 --> 35:08.720
But she was already in love with someone else.

271
35:08.720 --> 35:11.640
She wanted to marry him...

272
35:13.840 --> 35:19.840
and give up everything for a simple life, without rank or power.

273
35:23.920 --> 35:29.400
She'd have to choose between duty and happiness.

274
35:31.080 --> 35:33.360
Would you let her live that way?

275
35:42.680 --> 35:44.400
If it were my daughter,

276
35:46.880 --> 35:49.520
I know I'd love her dearly.

277
35:54.400 --> 36:00.200
I'd want her to be happy. I'd let her live as she wished.

278
36:07.400 --> 36:09.800
Thank you.

279
36:09.800 --> 36:15.040
Talking to you has put my mind at ease.

280
36:19.520 --> 36:21.760
I'm worried about my cousin.

281
36:23.320 --> 36:25.600
How is she?

282
36:31.360 --> 36:35.520
What's done is done.

283
36:41.960 --> 36:46.880
As for what lies ahead, we must do our best.

284
36:48.320 --> 36:51.280
Don't worry about your cousin.

285
36:51.280 --> 36:56.760
Leave what we've discussed here, and focus on your duties.

286
36:58.280 --> 37:04.280
I'll do the same and take good care of your cousin.

287
37:49.840 --> 37:55.080
The King summoned me and reprimanded me for failing to catch the rice bandits.

288
37:55.080 --> 37:58.480
Merng Mang's soldiers had to step in.

289
37:58.480 --> 38:01.600
But my men at the border insist...

290
38:01.600 --> 38:04.840
they've heard nothing of any rice bandits.

291
38:04.840 --> 38:06.920
If the bandits were real,

292
38:06.920 --> 38:10.840
my men would've known about them before Merng Mang's soldiers did.

293
38:16.160 --> 38:21.560
Whenever I visit the border, I hear nothing about these rice bandits.

294
38:21.560 --> 38:26.920
If our soldiers were patrolling there, they would've arrived first.

295
38:27.600 --> 38:29.400
It's humiliating.

296
38:29.400 --> 38:34.360
Merng Mang's soldiers catching bandits before ours?

297
38:34.360 --> 38:37.880
- It's unacceptable. - I find it strange, too.

298
38:37.880 --> 38:41.080
Why would Merng Mang's soldiers suddenly start catching bandits for us?

299
38:41.080 --> 38:43.120
Maybe they weren't bandits at all.

300
38:44.040 --> 38:45.960
Perhaps there's been a misunderstanding.

301
38:52.080 --> 38:55.000
What if someone deliberately misled us?

302
39:07.080 --> 39:09.280
If Fah Haam is right,

303
39:09.280 --> 39:15.000
Indraraja was the one who told Father and sought recognition for Prince Pha Wiang.

304
39:15.000 --> 39:16.760
I doubt he's entirely unaware.

305
39:16.760 --> 39:20.200
Come now, Saen Thep. Of course he knows.

306
39:20.200 --> 39:23.920
If he knew and went along with it, then he was part of the deception.

307
39:23.920 --> 39:26.320
I don't want to think that way,

308
39:26.320 --> 39:31.440
but I suspect Prince Pha Wiang is involved.

309
39:31.440 --> 39:35.520
If Prince Pha Wiang lied, Indraraja must know about it.

310
39:35.520 --> 39:36.880
Don't you agree?

311
39:39.320 --> 39:43.520
Everyone knows Ullavee's army is stronger than Merng Mang's.

312
39:43.520 --> 39:47.240
If they truly were bandits, our soldiers couldn't have missed them.

313
39:58.760 --> 40:01.600
What are those two plotting?

314
40:08.600 --> 40:10.040
Could it be that...

315
40:13.920 --> 40:16.120
Indraraja deliberately lied?

316
40:20.880 --> 40:22.560
Forgive me, Your Highness.

317
40:31.640 --> 40:34.480
You're all gathered here.

318
40:35.680 --> 40:38.640
Is there something I should know?

319
41:36.440 --> 41:37.640
Fongnuan!

320
41:38.880 --> 41:40.320
Yes, Your Highness?

321
41:42.040 --> 41:46.760
If you hadn't stopped me, I'd have kept talking.

322
41:46.760 --> 41:50.280
I'd have gotten into trouble with Indraraja and Prince Pha Wiang.

323
41:51.000 --> 41:53.280
That's what friends are for.

324
41:53.960 --> 41:56.960
You helped me before. I understand.

325
41:56.960 --> 42:00.040
But if you keep helping everyone with every little thing,

326
42:00.040 --> 42:03.200
you might lose your head.

327
42:03.200 --> 42:04.600
Understood.

328
42:07.240 --> 42:10.160
I owe you one.

329
42:10.160 --> 42:14.960
If you ever need my help, just say the word. I'll gladly help.

330
42:14.960 --> 42:18.280
Then do me a favor.

331
42:18.280 --> 42:22.480
Pay attention to who's around before you speak.

332
42:23.200 --> 42:26.160
I'd better finish cleaning up before I get scolded.

333
42:26.160 --> 42:27.320
Please excuse me.

334
42:50.320 --> 42:53.400
The tea and dessert you prepared today...

335
42:55.360 --> 42:57.600
weren't to my liking.

336
42:57.600 --> 42:58.640
Really?

337
42:58.640 --> 43:03.680
But Prince Jom Harn told me you liked rose tea and steamed banana cake.

338
43:10.520 --> 43:13.040
So you asked Jom Harn about my preferences.

339
43:14.880 --> 43:17.640
I just wanted to thank you...

340
43:17.640 --> 43:21.400
for showing me the way to Wat Khao Nam Saeng the other day.

341
43:25.640 --> 43:31.160
Actually, I like lotus tea and steamed banana cake.

342
43:35.840 --> 43:39.600
I like blue, but I don't like black.

343
43:41.720 --> 43:44.840
I like mangoes, but not vegetables.

344
43:44.840 --> 43:48.840
I like Hung Lay Curry. I don't like spicy food.

345
43:48.840 --> 43:54.840
I don't like getting drunk. I prefer the scent of lotus to jasmine.

346
43:55.640 --> 43:59.840
I prefer rainy days to hot weather.

347
44:03.240 --> 44:08.040
I don't like seeing people cry. I hate insincere people.

348
44:17.040 --> 44:22.080
Next time, don't ask anyone else. If you want to know something, ask me.

349
44:42.880 --> 44:46.960
How did senior get it so wrong? He's hopeless.

350
44:46.960 --> 44:48.200
He gave me away.

351
45:10.640 --> 45:12.080
Where do you think you're going?

352
45:17.080 --> 45:21.640
I met with my brothers today about the rice thefts at the border.

353
45:21.640 --> 45:25.160
I'd like to investigate this myself.

354
45:26.600 --> 45:28.160
I forbid you to go.

355
45:35.920 --> 45:39.120
Why, Mother? This is a serious matter.

356
45:39.120 --> 45:44.440
If we don't put a stop to these bandits, they'll raid our granaries again.

357
45:44.440 --> 45:48.160
We'll run short of rice, and our people will suffer.

358
45:50.360 --> 45:54.120
If you keep working all the time, when will you find a wife?

359
45:58.640 --> 46:00.760
- A wife? - Yes.

360
46:02.200 --> 46:07.600
This is important. You need a consort to please your father.

361
46:13.800 --> 46:18.560
If no one has caught your eye, I'll find someone for you.

362
46:22.240 --> 46:24.480
Leave the border matter alone for now.

363
46:26.160 --> 46:27.440
I've arranged for you

364
46:27.440 --> 46:30.760
to meet daughters of noble and prominent families.

365
46:34.760 --> 46:36.920
Don't embarrass me.

366
46:48.440 --> 46:53.160
Pha Wiang has already caught the rice bandits.

367
46:53.160 --> 46:55.160
That should've settled the matter.

368
46:56.280 --> 46:58.280
Why discuss it again?

369
47:01.480 --> 47:03.880
Muen In called everyone together...

370
47:03.880 --> 47:05.760
to discuss

371
47:05.760 --> 47:09.880
why Ullavee's soldiers at the border knew nothing about the rice thefts.

372
47:10.760 --> 47:13.520
When Pha Wiang and I entered the Royal Library,

373
47:13.520 --> 47:15.760
why did everyone fall silent?

374
47:17.600 --> 47:21.120
Muen In must be embarrassed...

375
47:21.120 --> 47:26.040
that Ullavee's soldiers failed to secure the border.

376
47:26.040 --> 47:30.160
He's probably trying to avoid blame by placing it on someone else.

377
47:30.160 --> 47:35.720
Seeing us together must have left him too ashamed to speak his mind.

378
47:35.720 --> 47:36.760
As for the others,

379
47:36.760 --> 47:41.360
I doubt they wanted to trouble you over such a minor matter.

380
47:42.120 --> 47:43.480
That seems likely.

381
47:43.480 --> 47:47.280
No wonder they fell silent, and didn't know what to say.

382
47:47.280 --> 47:49.240
Your influence must have intimidated them.

383
47:51.720 --> 47:53.360
We mustn't let our guard down.

384
47:54.360 --> 47:57.440
Everyone in Wiang Kaew is watching us.

385
47:57.440 --> 48:01.400
We must watch what we say and do.

386
48:22.520 --> 48:24.760
Under the circumstances,

387
48:24.760 --> 48:30.480
I'm sure you know what you should and shouldn't say.

388
48:34.520 --> 48:35.920
Don't worry.

389
48:36.640 --> 48:39.360
I won't get myself into trouble.

390
48:40.680 --> 48:45.160
You'd better not cause trouble for Indraraja either.

391
48:46.160 --> 48:48.960
Or I won't be the only one without a homeland.

392
48:52.960 --> 48:58.400
The throne of Merng Mang could slip from your grasp as well.

393
49:30.800 --> 49:32.200
Mother.

394
49:33.200 --> 49:35.040
Is this really necessary?

395
49:38.280 --> 49:42.440
I'm finding you a consort. I won't let you be outdone.

396
49:47.640 --> 49:51.240
This is Ked Kaew. She's Saen Inta's daughter.

397
49:51.240 --> 49:53.760
Her family has held the title of Supreme Minister

398
49:53.760 --> 49:54.960
for generations.

399
49:54.960 --> 50:00.680
If you take her as your consort, her family will give you great support.

400
50:06.800 --> 50:10.160
This is La-ong Kham. She's Muen Kaew's daughter.

401
50:10.160 --> 50:11.920
Her father is the Senior Military Minister.

402
50:11.920 --> 50:14.120
His rank is below the Supreme Minister's,

403
50:14.120 --> 50:17.400
but his family comes from a long line of royal artisans

404
50:17.400 --> 50:19.560
and is highly respected.

405
50:24.160 --> 50:26.280
This is Bua Wai.

406
50:26.280 --> 50:31.640
Her father is Kham Tan, the wealthiest merchant in Ullavee.

407
50:31.640 --> 50:35.360
Her family may not be of noble birth,

408
50:37.200 --> 50:42.440
but her wealth would certainly benefit you.

409
50:48.160 --> 50:52.880
All these women come from influential families that could support you.

410
50:54.320 --> 50:56.840
Whichever one you choose,

411
50:56.840 --> 51:00.160
she'll be just as worthy as Saen Thep's consort.

412
51:20.840 --> 51:25.520
You can't escape it, however hard you try. How can anyone live without love?

413
51:30.240 --> 51:31.560
True.

414
51:32.160 --> 51:36.000
But being in love doesn't mean you'll get what you want.

415
51:36.000 --> 51:40.040
Every time I fall in love, I end up disappointed.

416
51:40.040 --> 51:45.840
At least neither of you is being controlled like I am.

417
51:45.840 --> 51:49.720
Didn't any of the women Royal Consort Sukantha chose for you

418
51:49.720 --> 51:51.680
catch your eye?

419
51:53.080 --> 51:54.600
I don't know...

420
51:54.600 --> 52:00.360
what it feels like to be attracted to someone or to fall in love.

421
52:02.240 --> 52:06.040
Could you two explain how I can tell...

422
52:06.040 --> 52:09.840
whether I'm in love?

423
52:11.320 --> 52:13.280
It's simple.

424
52:13.280 --> 52:17.120
You meet someone you can't get out of your mind.

425
52:22.520 --> 52:28.280
Whether you're asleep or awake, eating or resting, you keep thinking of them.

426
52:28.960 --> 52:32.960
When they smile, you smile too.

427
52:32.960 --> 52:37.160
When they laugh, you laugh too.

428
52:38.560 --> 52:43.880
If I had to choose between falling in love and catching bandits,

429
52:46.240 --> 52:48.280
I'd rather hunt bandits.

430
52:50.280 --> 52:52.200
I'm off to the border.

431
52:56.440 --> 52:57.720
Jom Harn!

432
53:06.240 --> 53:08.120
Lady Fongnuan.

433
53:11.680 --> 53:14.120
Where's my cousin? How is she?

434
53:14.120 --> 53:17.640
Please go upstairs, my lady. Prince Saen Thep is waiting.

435
53:40.880 --> 53:42.600
Cousin.

436
53:50.160 --> 53:51.760
What's wrong with her?

437
53:53.240 --> 53:55.120
Ever since Maneethip heard the news,

438
53:57.000 --> 53:59.520
she hasn't left her room.

439
54:00.400 --> 54:02.240
She refuses to eat.

440
54:16.320 --> 54:17.720
Cousin.

441
54:26.120 --> 54:27.720
Fongnuan.

442
54:28.520 --> 54:31.880
I heard you weren't feeling well,

443
54:31.880 --> 54:35.240
so I asked Lady Homjan for permission to come and care for you.

444
54:36.800 --> 54:41.800
Please eat something and take your medicine. You'll feel better soon.

445
54:46.480 --> 54:48.440
I have no appetite.

446
55:07.760 --> 55:10.040
Stay here and keep her company.

447
55:10.960 --> 55:15.040
I'll bring some snacks and a fresh dose of medicine.

448
55:21.000 --> 55:26.480
Seeing you might give her the strength to get up and eat.

449
56:47.680 --> 56:50.160
Where are all the maids?

450
56:55.520 --> 56:59.080
I sent them to prepare her medicine and to the market...

451
56:59.080 --> 57:03.120
for Maneethip's favorite fruits and snacks.

452
57:05.520 --> 57:10.360
I've come to get some warm water. I want to give her a sponge bath.

453
57:13.760 --> 57:15.320
Your Highness!

454
57:16.360 --> 57:21.640
Let me have a look. I'll put some ointment on it.

455
57:34.600 --> 57:39.360
Thank you on Maneethip's behalf.

456
57:47.960 --> 57:50.000
Why are you thanking me?

457
57:51.440 --> 57:54.280
Even though she's hurt you,

458
57:56.320 --> 57:59.000
you're still taking such good care of her.

459
58:01.360 --> 58:04.040
How could I not thank you?

460
58:09.800 --> 58:12.520
I've hurt her too.

461
58:14.440 --> 58:17.080
She may be suffering more than I am.

462
58:18.840 --> 58:20.840
Her grief has made her ill.

463
58:27.880 --> 58:30.840
I'm truly grateful, Your Highness.

464
58:38.880 --> 58:43.760
I can't change what's happened.

465
58:47.320 --> 58:49.560
But from this day forward,

466
58:51.800 --> 58:57.200
I'll do everything I can to take good care of Maneethip.

467
59:00.480 --> 59:02.280
Once she recovers,

468
59:05.040 --> 59:07.400
whatever she decides,

469
59:10.520 --> 59:12.080
I'll accept her decision.

470
59:17.760 --> 59:19.160
In that case,

471
59:20.960 --> 59:24.360
let's do everything we can for her...

472
59:25.080 --> 59:30.320
and help her get well as soon as possible.

473
59:43.880 --> 59:45.800
Once upon a time, in a forest,

474
59:47.040 --> 59:50.880
all the animals lived together in harmony.

475
01:01:06.720 --> 01:01:10.320
[Next Week] You have a lot on your mind right now,

476
01:01:10.320 --> 01:01:11.920
especially about your cousin.

477
01:01:11.920 --> 01:01:13.600
You've been looking after everyone else.

478
01:01:13.600 --> 01:01:15.320
Don't forget to take care of yourself.

479
01:01:15.320 --> 01:01:17.200
Whatever the future holds,

480
01:01:17.200 --> 01:01:22.320
I'll devote the rest of my life to taking good care of you and your cousin.

481
01:01:23.720 --> 01:01:26.840
I'm sorry I wasn't there for you when you were suffering.

482
01:01:26.840 --> 01:01:29.280
Dao Kaew. Don't you remember me?

483
01:01:29.280 --> 01:01:30.520
You're that drunkard.

484
01:01:30.520 --> 01:01:34.120
You asked Lady Homjan to arrange for me to teach you music, didn't you?

485
01:01:34.120 --> 01:01:37.200
- Yes. - Do you want to see me more often?

486
01:01:37.200 --> 01:01:39.640
Princess Maneethip's condition has grown much worse.
